    Janitor: retain whole .elan tree (restore nested toolchain patterns)
    
    A case pattern matches the WHOLE path, so '*/.elan' does not cover
    '.elan/toolchains' or '.elan/toolchains/<toolchain>'. Use a single
    alternation pattern */.elan|*/.elan/toolchains|*/.elan/toolchains/* so the
    entire live Lean/elAN toolchain tree is retained (J2), not just the top-level
    elan home. Restores tests/janitor-smoke.sh to green.

diff --git a/government/janitor.sh b/government/janitor.sh
index 52ff8c08..42939c21 100644
--- a/government/janitor.sh
+++ b/government/janitor.sh
@@ -415,12 +415,12 @@ classify() {
                 fi
             fi
             ;;
-        */.elan)
+        */.elan|*/.elan/toolchains|*/.elan/toolchains/*)
             # Live Lean/elAN toolchain installation (elan home: toolchains, the
             # elan binary, settings). Quarantining it breaks the Lean build until
             # elan re-downloads the pinned toolchain (failure mode J2: live build
             # dependency). The directory mtime ages after install, so age is not
-            # an abandonment signal here; retain it.
+            # an abandonment signal here; retain the whole tree.
             class=retain
             ;;
         *)
